  "body": "## The remaining blocker (found by the live test)\n\nThe rename-then-reinstall handled the tool dir (Windows lets you rename a dir a process runs from), but `uv tool install` then failed copying the **launcher shims** in `~/.local/bin`:\n```\nfailed to copy ...\\my-claude-code\\Scripts\\fcc-claude.exe to ...\\.local\\bin\\fcc-claude.exe:\nThe process cannot access the file because it is being used by another process. (os error 32)\n```\nA running launcher holds its own `.exe` shim **without `FILE_SHARE_DELETE`**, so it cannot be overwritten or renamed (verified: 5 attempts, all os error 32). \"Running in memory\" doesn't bypass this — the lock is on the open handle's share mode.\n\n## Why it's solvable\n\nThe shim is **version-agnostic**: its embedded `__main__.py` shebangs to the absolute tool-dir python path and imports the entrypoint. It does NOT embed a version. So a locked shim does not need updating — a new launch of it already resolves the fresh tool dir after the rename+reinstall.\n\n## The fix (community-canonical)\n\nThe uv maintainers (uv#14520) and real updaters (Microsoft conductor, hermes-agent) use: **\"move the running executables into a temporary directory\" before installing.** This PR does exactly that:\n\n1. Rename the tool dir aside (already in place).\n2. **Rename every launcher shim aside** (best-effort — the ~17 free ones succeed; the ~3 locked ones held by active windows fail and stay, which is fine).\n3. `uv tool install` writes a fresh tool env + fresh shims at the canonical paths.\n4. Open windows keep old code; new windows/servers get the new version.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Free shims rename OK; running-shim rename fails (expected, harmless).\n- All 7 rename + deferred tests pass; ruff/ty clean.\n- **Live test pending post-merge** via the published URL (serves `main`).\n\nVersion 5.3.2 → 5.3.3.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
