    "message": "fix(install): rename launcher shims aside so uv can install fresh while windows open\n\nuv writes the mcc-*/fcc-* launcher shims (PE+zipapp executables) into the uv\ntool bin dir. A running launcher holds its own .exe WITHOUT FILE_SHARE_DELETE,\nso uv cannot overwrite that one shim -- os error 32. But the shim is\nversion-agnostic (its __main__.py shebangs to the absolute tool-dir python path\nand imports the entrypoint), so it does not need updating: a new launch of it\nalready resolves the fresh tool dir after the rename+reinstall.\n\nThe rename-then-reinstall path now also renames every launcher shim aside\n(best-effort; locked ones fail and stay) before `uv tool install`, so uv writes\nfresh shims at the canonical paths for the free ones. Open windows keep old\ncode; new windows/servers get the new version -- the requirement.\n\nVerified live: free shims rename OK; running-shim rename fails (expected, and\nharmless); the community-canonical \"move running executables aside\" approach\n(uv#14520, conductor, hermes) is what this implements. All 7 rename+deferred\ntests pass; ruff/ty clean.\n\nVersion 5.3.2 -> 5.3.3.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
